course: dictionary
lesson: 9331
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and spin is one of them. The meaning that fits depends on the sentence around it. Look at the clues: what is spinning, and why? «The Earth spins once about every 24 hours» tells you spin means turning round, because the Earth turns, it does not make thread.
explain: Now read «Spiders spin webs from silk.» Here spin means to make something by twisting fibres. The word around it, webs, is the clue. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Spin can also be a noun, as in «go for a spin», which means a short ride for fun. It can even mean a false way of telling a story: «spin means choosing nice-sounding words to make something bad sound good». Same word, different job, so the clues decide which meaning you need.
fact: Spin is a verb and a noun: you can spin a top, or go for a spin.
fact: «Spin» means to turn round and round quickly.
fact: «Spin» can also mean to make thread by twisting fibres, as people did on spinning wheels to make yarn from wool.
fact: «My head is spinning» means you feel dizzy or confused.
fact: «Spin» can mean choosing nice-sounding words to make something bad sound good.
exercise: «As the Earth spins, every place is carried from the dark half into the light half.» What does spins mean here? | Feels dizzy | *Turns round and round | Goes for a short ride | Makes thread from wool
exercise: «Darwin's bark spider spins webs across rivers.» What does spins mean here? | Turns round quickly like a top | Goes for a fun ride | Feels confused | *Makes a web by twisting silk
exercise: Mia says, «I'm going for a spin on my bike.» What does spin mean here? | A story told to make something sound good | Turning on one foot | A web made of silk | *A short ride for fun
test: «My head is spinning after the fair ride.» What does spinning mean here? | Making thread from wool | Going for a fast car ride | *Feeling dizzy or confused | Turning a top on the table
test: Ben says the politician's words are spin, because they choose nice-sounding words to make bad news sound good. What does spin mean here? | A short ride in a car | Making thread by twisting fibres | *Choosing nice-sounding words to make bad news sound good | Turning round and round quickly
exam: Which meaning of spin is in «people spun wool into yarn on spinning wheels»? | *Make thread by twisting fibres | To turn round quickly | A short ride for fun | To feel dizzy
